# =============================================================================
# Docker build-context exclusions — mirror of the repository-root .dockerignore
# =============================================================================
# Both MeetFlow images are built from the repository root (`context: ..`),
# because the npm workspace tree — root package.json, package-lock.json and the
# server/client/e2e workspaces — must all be inside the build context. Docker
# therefore reads ../.dockerignore, not this file.
#
# This copy exists so the rules travel with the container definitions and so a
# build run with docker/ as its context still excludes the same things. Keep it
# byte-identical in intent to ../.dockerignore.
# =============================================================================

# --- Dependencies ------------------------------------------------------------
# Reinstalled inside the image from package-lock.json so the tree matches the
# image's platform and Node version rather than the developer's laptop.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.npm
.pnp
.pnp.js

# --- Build output ------------------------------------------------------------
# The builder stage compiles its own; a stale host dist silently shipping to
# production is exactly the failure this prevents.
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Version control / CI ----------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime configuration is injected as environment variables. A .env baked into
# a layer is readable by anyone who can pull the image, and src/config/env.ts
# would happily load it in preference to nothing.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# --- Tests, fixtures and their artefacts -------------------------------------
# Never executed in a container, and leaving them out stops seeded test data
# from being mistaken for production data.
tests
**/tests
coverage
**/coverage
.nyc_output
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
.playwright
**/*.test.ts
**/*.spec.ts
**/vitest.config.ts
**/playwright.config.ts

# --- Documentation -----------------------------------------------------------
docs
*.md
**/*.md

# --- Local infrastructure ----------------------------------------------------
# Compose files are read by the Docker CLI, not by a build. docker/volumes is
# host state. docker/ itself stays in the context: client.Dockerfile copies
# docker/nginx.conf.
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
docker/volumes
volumes
.tmp

# --- Editor / OS noise -------------------------------------------------------
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
logs
*.log
